{
  "readme": [
    "Canonical-body vectors for the operator act page (astra-plugins-ops dev/operator-acts-by-passkey-design.md §3.1) and the registry's verifier (bot/lib/operator-act.mjs).",
    "`valid[].canonical` is the exact UTF-8 text of `canonical(value)`: keys sorted (JS default order) at every level, no whitespace, JSON.stringify's escaping, values strings, arrays of strings or objects. `challenge` is base64url(SHA-256(canonical)), the WebAuthn challenge.",
    "`invalid[].text` must each be refused: no value parses to an object whose canonical form is that exact text.",
    "`fingerprints[]`: the first 16 hex of SHA-256 of the bytes `public_key` decodes to, in four groups of four. Neither is a real key.",
    "Generated once from bot/lib/operator-act.mjs; bot/tests/operator-act.test.mjs holds this file to it."
  ],
